  "domain": "security",
  "definition": "Iris recognition is a biometric identification technique that authenticates individuals from the intricate, epigenetically random texture of the iris, which is stable from early childhood and differs even between genetically identical twins. Near-infrared imaging, iris segmentation and Gabor-wavelet encoding \u2014 pioneered by John Daugman \u2014 produce a compact IrisCode compared via Hamming distance, delivering among the lowest false-match rates of any biometric and powering border control, national identity schemes such as India's Aadhaar, and proof-of-personhood systems.",
